<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>DOM XSS</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"></head>
<body><main class="wrap">
  <a href="/">← Lab home</a><p class="eyebrow">CHALLENGE 03</p><h1>DOM-based XSS</h1>
  <p>This page reads the URL fragment and inserts it into the DOM using <code>innerHTML</code>.</p>
  <p>Try adding <code>#hello</code> to the URL, then inspect how the page uses it.</p>
  <section class="result"><h2>Fragment output</h2><div id="output" class="unsafe-output">Nothing loaded yet.</div></section>
  <details><summary>Learning notes</summary><p>Try a harmless payload such as <code>#&lt;img src=x onerror=alert('DOM-XSS')&gt;</code>. The fragment is processed in the browser and is not sent to the server in the HTTP request.</p></details>
  <script>
    // INTENTIONALLY VULNERABLE: for local training only.
    const fragment = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1));
    if (fragment) document.getElementById("output").innerHTML = fragment;
  </script>
</main></body></html>